# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. NEVER committed.
#
# The source panel is ~298MB (over GitHub's 100MB hard limit) and contains
# personal data on ~50,000 named real estate agents. The scored outputs carry
# per-person churn-risk and income predictions against real names. Neither
# belongs in version control, private repo or not.
# See README.md "Getting the data".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.csv
!docs/schema/*.csv
# Aggregate recalibration history -- no agent-level data, and it is the evidence
# trail for what each quarterly run actually did.
!MA/recalibration_log.csv

# Scored production outputs and their backups (named agents + predictions)
current_agent_risk_scores.csv*
current_agent_sales_forecast.csv*
agent_explanations*.csv
leave_risk_scores.csv
*.uuid_keyed_backup

# Point-in-time backups of source files. Useful locally while editing; noise in
# a repository that already keeps full history.
*_backup
*.backup

# Generated reports containing agent names
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environments, caches, build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Model training scratch
catboost_info/
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded working directories, kept locally, not part of the project
#
# These held RI's code before the 2026-09-01 state-major reorganisation and
# now hold only the virtualenv, retired dataset copies, and research scratch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Likelihood_to_Leave_Algorithm/
Forecasted_Sales_Algorithm/
Coaching_Score_Algorithm/
